  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(\\log_7(\\log_3(\\log_2x))=0,\\) then \\(x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\) equals",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\frac13\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\frac1{2\\sqrt3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\frac1{3\\sqrt3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac1{\\sqrt{42}}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1983-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The equation gives \\(\\log_3(\\log_2x)=1,\\) so \\(\\log_2x=3\\) and \\(x=8.\\) Hence \\(x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt8}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt2},\\) which is not among choices A–D.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Undo the logarithms one at a time, starting from the outside",
        "\\(\\log_7u=0\\) implies \\(u=1,\\) then continue inward"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
